# Native Android rules (Kotlin/Java, AndroidManifest.xml, Gradle, res/)
# Generated from the threat library cards (threats/android/*); each rule cites its card.
# Fields (tab-separated, "-" = empty):
#   rule_id threat_id severity type file_globs pattern message card flags [exclude]
# Severity: high/critical block the build by default; medium/low warn.
# Heuristic rules are kept one level below the card severity so they warn.
AND-EXP-001	android-exported-components	high	check	AndroidManifest.xml	manifest;;exported_unprotected;;activity|activity-alias|receiver	Component is exported with no permission: set android:exported="false", or protect it with a signature-level android:permission and validate every incoming intent	android/exported-components.md	-
AND-EXP-002	android-exported-components	high	check	AndroidManifest.xml	manifest;;implicit_export;;activity|activity-alias|service|receiver	Component has an intent-filter but no android:exported: set it explicitly (false unless other apps must reach it)	android/exported-components.md	-
AND-EXP-003	android-exported-components	medium	check	*.kt;*.java	call;;(^|[^A-Za-z_])registerReceiver\(;;!RECEIVER_NOT_EXPORTED|LocalBroadcastManager	Runtime receiver may be exported: pass ContextCompat.RECEIVER_NOT_EXPORTED unless other apps must send to it	android/exported-components.md	-
AND-CP-001	android-contentprovider-vulnerabilities	high	check	AndroidManifest.xml	manifest;;exported_unprotected;;provider	ContentProvider is exported with no read/write permission: set exported="false" or enforce signature-level permissions	android/ipc/android-contentprovider-vulnerabilities.md	-
AND-CP-002	sql-injection	high	match	*.kt;*.java	(rawQuery|execSQL)\([[:space:]]*"[^"]*("[[:space:]]*\+|\$\{?[A-Za-z_])	SQL built by string concatenation/templates: use selectionArgs / bind parameters (or Room queries)	shared/injection/sql-injection.md	-
AND-CP-003	path-traversal	medium	check	*.kt;*.java	cooccur;;openFile\(;;(uri|it)\.(path|lastPathSegment|getPath\(\)|getLastPathSegment\(\));;!canonicalPath|getCanonicalPath|canonicalFile|getCanonicalFile|normalize\(\)	Heuristic: provider openFile() builds a path from the URI without canonicalizing it; resolve getCanonicalPath() and confirm it stays inside the allowed directory	shared/injection/path-traversal.md	-
AND-FP-001	android-fileprovider-misconfig	high	match	res/xml/*.xml	<root-path	FileProvider <root-path> shares the whole filesystem: share only a dedicated subdirectory	android/ipc/android-fileprovider-misconfig.md	-
AND-FP-002	android-fileprovider-misconfig	medium	match	res/xml/*.xml	<(files|cache|external|external-files|external-cache|external-media)-path[^>]*path="(\.|/)?"	FileProvider path shares an entire storage root: narrow path to a dedicated subdirectory	android/ipc/android-fileprovider-misconfig.md	-
AND-FP-003	android-fileprovider-misconfig	medium	match	*.kt;*.java	FLAG_GRANT_(WRITE|PERSISTABLE|PREFIX)_URI_PERMISSION	Broad URI grant (write / persistable / prefix): grant read-only, per-URI, short-lived access instead	android/ipc/android-fileprovider-misconfig.md	-
AND-FP-004	android-fileprovider-misconfig	high	check	AndroidManifest.xml	manifest;;fileprovider_exported	FileProvider must not be exported: set android:exported="false" and grant per-URI permissions	android/ipc/android-fileprovider-misconfig.md	-
AND-IR-001	android-intent-redirection	medium	check	*.kt;*.java	cooccur;;getParcelableExtra<Intent>|getParcelableExtra\([^)]*Intent(::class|\.class)|\(Intent\)[^;]*getParcelableExtra|Intent\.parseUri\(;;(startActivity|startService|sendBroadcast|setResult)\(;;!IntentSanitizer|resolveActivity|callingPackage|getCallingPackage	Heuristic: an Intent taken from extras is launched; validate its component/package (androidx IntentSanitizer) before starting it	android/ipc/android-intent-redirection.md	-
AND-IR-002	android-intent-redirection	high	match	*.kt;*.java	removeLaunchSecurityProtection\(	removeLaunchSecurityProtection() disables unsafe-intent-launch protection: remove it and sanitize the nested intent	android/ipc/android-intent-redirection.md	-
AND-IS-001	android-intent-spoofing	medium	match	*.kt;*.java	(^|[^A-Za-z_])sendBroadcast\([[:space:]]*[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*[[:space:]]*\)	Broadcast sent without a receiver permission: use an explicit intent (setPackage) or sendBroadcast(intent, permission)	android/ipc/android-intent-spoofing.md	-	LocalBroadcastManager
AND-IS-002	android-intent-spoofing	medium	check	*.kt;*.java	cooccur;;putExtra\([[:space:]]*"[^"]*([Tt]oken|[Pp]assword|[Ss]ession|OTP|[Oo]tp|TOKEN|PASSWORD|SESSION);;Intent\([[:space:]]*("|Intent\.ACTION_|ACTION_);;!setPackage\(|setComponent\(|setClass\(|setClassName\(|\.package[[:space:]]*=	Heuristic: sensitive extras on an implicit intent can be intercepted; make the intent explicit (setPackage / setComponent)	android/ipc/android-intent-spoofing.md	-
AND-PI-001	android-pendingintent-hijacking	high	check	*.kt;*.java	call;;PendingIntent\.get(Activity|Activities|Service|ForegroundService|Broadcast)\(;;!FLAG_IMMUTABLE	PendingIntent without FLAG_IMMUTABLE can be filled in by another app: add PendingIntent.FLAG_IMMUTABLE and an explicit base intent	android/ipc/android-pendingintent-hijacking.md	-
AND-PI-002	android-pendingintent-hijacking	medium	match	*.kt;*.java	FLAG_MUTABLE	Mutable PendingIntent: only use FLAG_MUTABLE when required (inline reply, bubbles) and always with an explicit base intent	android/ipc/android-pendingintent-hijacking.md	-
AND-TH-001	android-task-hijacking	medium	match	AndroidManifest.xml	android:taskAffinity="[^"]+"|android:allowTaskReparenting="true"	Custom taskAffinity / allowTaskReparenting enables task hijacking (StrandHogg): set android:taskAffinity="" on <application> unless required	android/ipc/android-task-hijacking.md	-
AND-BD-001	android-unsafe-binder-aidl	high	check	AndroidManifest.xml	manifest;;exported_unprotected;;service	Service is exported with no permission: set exported="false" or require a signature permission, and check Binder.getCallingUid() in the binder	android/ipc/android-unsafe-binder-aidl.md	-
AND-BD-002	android-unsafe-binder-aidl	medium	match	*.kt;*.java	(check|enforce)CallingOrSelfPermission\(	*CallingOrSelfPermission passes when your own app holds the permission: use checkCallingPermission / enforceCallingPermission	android/ipc/android-unsafe-binder-aidl.md	-
AND-PM-001	android-custom-permission-misconfig	medium	match	AndroidManifest.xml	android:protectionLevel="(normal|dangerous)"	Custom permission with normal/dangerous protection: use protectionLevel="signature" for app-to-app access	android/permissions/android-custom-permission-misconfig.md	-
AND-PM-002	android-custom-permission-misconfig	medium	check	AndroidManifest.xml	manifest;;permission_no_level	<permission> without protectionLevel defaults to normal (any app can hold it): set protectionLevel="signature"	android/permissions/android-custom-permission-misconfig.md	-
AND-PM-003	android-custom-permission-misconfig	high	match	AndroidManifest.xml	android:permission="(true|false)"	android:permission must name a permission, not a boolean: the component is effectively unprotected	android/permissions/android-custom-permission-misconfig.md	-
AND-PM-004	android-custom-permission-misconfig	low	check	AndroidManifest.xml	manifest;;undeclared_permission	Enforced permission is not declared here: declare it with protectionLevel="signature" (or confirm the declaring app is trusted) to avoid permission squatting	android/permissions/android-custom-permission-misconfig.md	-
AND-PM-005	android-excessive-permissions	low	check	AndroidManifest.xml	xml_element;;uses-permission;;android\.permission\.(READ_CONTACTS|ACCESS_BACKGROUND_LOCATION|READ_SMS|SEND_SMS|READ_CALL_LOG|MANAGE_EXTERNAL_STORAGE|QUERY_ALL_PACKAGES|READ_PHONE_STATE|READ_EXTERNAL_STORAGE|WRITE_EXTERNAL_STORAGE);;!tools:node="remove"	High-risk permission requested: confirm it is essential, or use the scoped alternative (photo picker, contact picker, SAF, package visibility <queries>)	android/permissions/android-excessive-permissions.md	-
AND-SR-001	android-sensor-radio-abuse	medium	check	AndroidManifest.xml	xml_element;;uses-permission;;android\.permission\.(BLUETOOTH_SCAN|NEARBY_WIFI_DEVICES);;!neverForLocation|tools:node="remove"	Bluetooth/Wi-Fi scan permission can derive location: add android:usesPermissionFlags="neverForLocation" if you do not need location	android/permissions/android-sensor-radio-abuse.md	-
AND-SMS-001	android-sms-interception	high	check	AndroidManifest.xml	xml_element;;uses-permission;;android\.permission\.(READ_SMS|RECEIVE_SMS|RECEIVE_MMS|RECEIVE_WAP_PUSH);;!tools:node="remove"	Reading SMS for OTPs exposes all messages: use the SMS Retriever / SMS User Consent API (or app-based MFA)	android/integrity/android-sms-interception.md	-
AND-SMS-002	android-sms-interception	high	match	*.kt;*.java;AndroidManifest.xml	SMS_RECEIVED	SMS broadcast receiver: replace with the SMS Retriever / User Consent API	android/integrity/android-sms-interception.md	-
AND-IC-001	android-input-capture	medium	check	res/layout*/*.xml	xml_element;;EditText|[A-Za-z0-9_.]*TextInputEditText|[A-Za-z0-9_.]*AppCompatEditText;;android:(id|hint)="[^"]*([Pp]assword|[Pp]asscode|[Cc]vv|CVV|[/_]otp|Otp|OTP|[/_]pin[_"]|PIN);;!inputType="[^"]*(textPassword|numberPassword|textWebPassword)"	Heuristic: secret field without a password inputType is visible, autocompleted and learned by keyboards; set inputType="textPassword" / "numberPassword" (and imeOptions flagNoPersonalizedLearning)	android/permissions/android-input-capture.md	-
AND-OV-001	android-overlay-tapjacking	low	tree-absent	*.kt;*.java;res/layout*/*.xml;AndroidManifest.xml	filterTouchesWhenObscured|setFilterTouchesWhenObscured|setHideOverlayWindows|HIDE_OVERLAY_WINDOWS|FLAG_SECURE|FLAG_WINDOW_IS_(PARTIALLY_)?OBSCURED	No overlay/tapjacking or screen-capture defense anywhere: protect sensitive screens with filterTouchesWhenObscured / setHideOverlayWindows(true) and FLAG_SECURE	android/permissions/android-overlay-tapjacking.md	-
AND-INT-001	android-apk-tampering-repackaging	low	tree-absent	*.kt;*.java;*.gradle;*.gradle.kts;*.dart;*.js;*.ts;*.tsx;pubspec.yaml;package.json	IntegrityManagerFactory|StandardIntegrityManager|play:integrity|play-integrity|SafetyNet|RootBeer|rootbeer|freerasp|JailMonkey|jail-monkey|flutter_jailbreak_detection|safe_device|Talsec	No app-integrity signal (Play Integrity or RASP) found: verify Play Integrity verdicts on your backend for sensitive actions	android/integrity/android-apk-tampering-repackaging.md	-
AND-DA-001	android-privileged-service-abuse	medium	match	AndroidManifest.xml	BIND_DEVICE_ADMIN|BIND_VPN_SERVICE|FOREGROUND_SERVICE_MEDIA_PROJECTION|BIND_ACCESSIBILITY_SERVICE	App requests a privileged service (device admin / VPN / media projection / accessibility): confirm it is essential and documented for Play policy	android/permissions/android-privileged-service-abuse.md	-
AND-BK-001	android-backup-exposure	medium	check	AndroidManifest.xml	xml_element;;application;;android:allowBackup="true";;!android:(dataExtractionRules|fullBackupContent)=	Backups are enabled with no rules: set allowBackup="false" or add dataExtractionRules / fullBackupContent that exclude tokens, keys and databases	android/storage/android-backup-exposure.md	-
AND-BK-002	android-backup-exposure	medium	check	AndroidManifest.xml	xml_element;;application;;android:(label|icon|name|theme)=;;!android:allowBackup=;;!android:(dataExtractionRules|fullBackupContent)=	<application> has no android:allowBackup (defaults to true) and no backup rules: set allowBackup="false" or add exclusion rules	android/storage/android-backup-exposure.md	-
AND-BK-003	android-backup-exposure	medium	match	res/xml/*.xml	<include[^>]*domain="(root|file|database|sharedpref)"[^>]*path="(\.|/)?"	Backup rule includes an entire data domain: include only non-sensitive paths and exclude credentials	android/storage/android-backup-exposure.md	-
AND-DL-001	android-data-leakage-surfaces	medium	check	*.kt;*.java	near;;(setPrimaryClip|ClipData\.newPlainText)\(;;1;;([Pp]assword|[Tt]oken|OTP|[Oo]tp|[Ss]ecret|PIN|[Cc]vv);;!IS_SENSITIVE	Sensitive value copied to the clipboard: avoid it, or mark the ClipData with EXTRA_IS_SENSITIVE (Android 13+) and clear it	android/storage/android-data-leakage-surfaces.md	-
AND-DL-002	android-data-leakage-surfaces	low	match	*.kt;*.java	VISIBILITY_PUBLIC	Public notification shows its content on the lock screen: use VISIBILITY_PRIVATE with setPublicVersion() for sensitive content	android/storage/android-data-leakage-surfaces.md	-	setPublicVersion
AND-SEC-001	android-hardcoded-secrets	high	match	*.gradle;*.gradle.kts;gradle.properties	buildConfigField[[:space:]]*\(?[[:space:]]*"String"[[:space:]]*,[[:space:]]*"[A-Za-z0-9_]*(KEY|SECRET|TOKEN|PASSWORD|Key|Secret|Token|Password)[A-Za-z0-9_]*"[[:space:]]*,[[:space:]]*"\\"[^"\\$]{8,}\\""	Secret literal compiled into BuildConfig: read it from an untracked properties file / CI secret, and keep real secrets on the server	android/storage/android-hardcoded-secrets.md	redact
AND-SEC-002	android-hardcoded-secrets	high	match	*.gradle;*.gradle.kts;gradle.properties	resValue[[:space:]]*\(?[[:space:]]*"string"[[:space:]]*,[[:space:]]*"[A-Za-z0-9_]*([Kk]ey|KEY|[Ss]ecret|SECRET|[Tt]oken|TOKEN)[A-Za-z0-9_]*"[[:space:]]*,[[:space:]]*"[^"$]{12,}"	Secret literal compiled into resources: inject it from an untracked source, and keep real secrets on the server	android/storage/android-hardcoded-secrets.md	redact
AND-SEC-003	android-hardcoded-secrets	high	imatch	res/values*/*.xml	<string[^>]*name="[^"]*(api_?key|secret|token|password|client_?secret)[^"]*"[^>]*>[^<[:space:]]{16,}</string>	Secret in string resources is trivially extracted from the APK: remove it and keep it server-side	android/storage/android-hardcoded-secrets.md	redact	>@|AIza|facebook_client_token
AND-SEC-004	signing-key-theft	high	match	*.gradle;*.gradle.kts;gradle.properties	(storePassword|keyPassword)[[:space:]]*(=|\()?[[:space:]]*["'][^"'$]+["']	Keystore password in the build script: load it from environment / ~/.gradle/gradle.properties / CI secrets	shared/supply-chain/signing-key-theft.md	redact	["']android["']
AND-ST-001	android-insecure-data-storage	medium	check	*.kt;*.java	cooccur;;putString\([[:space:]]*("[^"]*([Tt]oken|TOKEN|[Pp]assword|PASSWORD|[Ss]ecret|SECRET|[Jj]wt|JWT|[Ss]ession|SESSION)|[A-Z_]*(TOKEN|PASSWORD|SECRET|JWT|SESSION)[A-Z_]*[[:space:]]*,)|stringPreferencesKey\([[:space:]]*"[^"]*([Tt]oken|[Pp]assword|[Ss]ecret|[Jj]wt);;!EncryptedSharedPreferences|EncryptedFile|[Tt]ink|Aead|\.encrypt\(|encrypt[A-Z][A-Za-z]*\(	Heuristic: credential saved in plain SharedPreferences/DataStore; encrypt it with a Keystore-backed key (or keep only short-lived tokens)	android/storage/android-insecure-data-storage.md	-
AND-ST-002	android-insecure-data-storage	high	match	*.kt;*.java	MODE_WORLD_(READABLE|WRITEABLE)	World-readable/writable file mode exposes app data to every app: use MODE_PRIVATE	android/storage/android-insecure-data-storage.md	-
AND-ST-003	android-insecure-data-storage	low	match	*.kt;*.java	getExternalStorageDirectory|getExternalStoragePublicDirectory|getExternalFilesDir|getExternalCacheDir	External storage is readable by other apps / the user: keep sensitive files in internal storage (filesDir)	android/storage/android-insecure-data-storage.md	-
AND-ST-004	android-insecure-data-storage	medium	match	AndroidManifest.xml	requestLegacyExternalStorage="true"	Legacy external storage opts out of scoped storage: remove requestLegacyExternalStorage	android/storage/android-insecure-data-storage.md	-
AND-ST-005	android-keystore-misuse	low	match	*.gradle;*.gradle.kts;gradle.properties	androidx\.security:security-crypto	androidx.security:security-crypto (EncryptedSharedPreferences) is deprecated: migrate to a Keystore-backed key with Tink / Cipher	android/storage/android-keystore-misuse.md	-
AND-KS-001	android-keystore-misuse	medium	check	*.kt;*.java	cooccur;;KeyGenParameterSpec\.Builder;;!setUserAuthenticationRequired\([[:space:]]*true	Heuristic: Keystore key is usable without user authentication; for keys that protect secrets call setUserAuthenticationRequired(true)	android/storage/android-keystore-misuse.md	-
AND-KS-002	android-keystore-misuse	medium	match	*.kt;*.java	setInvalidatedByBiometricEnrollment\([[:space:]]*false	Key survives new biometric enrollment, so an added fingerprint unlocks it: keep the default (true)	android/storage/android-keystore-misuse.md	-
AND-KS-003	android-keystore-misuse	medium	match	*.kt;*.java	[Pp]rompt[A-Za-z]*\.authenticate\([[:space:]]*[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_.]*[[:space:]]*\)	BiometricPrompt without a CryptoObject is a UI check that hooking bypasses: authenticate(promptInfo, CryptoObject(cipher)) with a user-auth-bound key	android/storage/android-keystore-misuse.md	-	CryptoObject
AND-KS-004	android-keystore-misuse	medium	match	*.kt;*.java	KeyStore\.getInstance\([[:space:]]*"(BKS|PKCS12|JKS)"	Software keystore file instead of the hardware-backed AndroidKeyStore: generate keys in "AndroidKeyStore"	android/storage/android-keystore-misuse.md	-
AND-WV-001	android-webview-javascript-interface	high	match	*.kt;*.java	addJavascriptInterface\(	JavaScript bridge is exposed to every page the WebView loads: use WebViewCompat.addWebMessageListener with an origin allow-list, and load only trusted https content	android/webview/android-webview-javascript-interface.md	-
AND-WV-002	android-webview-javascript-interface	high	match	*.kt;*.java	(addWebMessageListener|postWebMessage)\(.*("\*"|Uri\.EMPTY)	Web message channel accepts any origin: restrict allowed origins to your exact https origins	android/webview/android-webview-javascript-interface.md	-
AND-WV-003	android-webview-untrusted-content	low	match	*.kt;*.java	setJavaScriptEnabled\([[:space:]]*true|javaScriptEnabled[[:space:]]*=[[:space:]]*true	JavaScript is enabled in a WebView: load only trusted https content and keep file access off	android/webview/android-webview-untrusted-content.md	-
AND-WV-004	android-webview-file-access	high	match	*.kt;*.java	(setAllowFileAccessFromFileURLs|setAllowUniversalAccessFromFileURLs)\([[:space:]]*true|(allowFileAccessFromFileURLs|allowUniversalAccessFromFileURLs)[[:space:]]*=[[:space:]]*true	file:// pages may read other files or any origin: keep these false and serve local content with WebViewAssetLoader	android/webview/android-webview-file-access.md	-
AND-WV-005	android-webview-file-access	high	match	*.kt;*.java	setAllowFileAccess\([[:space:]]*true|allowFileAccess[[:space:]]*=[[:space:]]*true	WebView file access is enabled: set it to false and use WebViewAssetLoader for bundled content	android/webview/android-webview-file-access.md	-
AND-WV-006	android-webview-file-access	high	match	*.kt;*.java	loadUrl\([[:space:]]*"file://	WebView loads a file:// URL: serve local content via WebViewAssetLoader (https://appassets.androidplatform.net)	android/webview/android-webview-file-access.md	-	file:///android_(asset|res)/
AND-WV-007	android-webview-tls-bypass	critical	check	*.kt;*.java	within;;onReceivedSslError;;\.proceed\(\)	onReceivedSslError calls proceed(): TLS errors are ignored. Call handler.cancel() and show an error	android/webview/android-webview-tls-bypass.md	-
AND-WV-008	android-webview-tls-bypass	high	match	*.kt;*.java	MIXED_CONTENT_(ALWAYS_ALLOW|COMPATIBILITY_MODE)	Mixed content lets http resources into https pages: keep MIXED_CONTENT_NEVER_ALLOW	android/webview/android-webview-tls-bypass.md	-
AND-WV-009	android-webview-tls-bypass	high	check	res/xml/*.xml	xml_element;;base-config|domain-config;;cleartextTrafficPermitted="true";;!<domain[^>]*>(localhost|10\.0\.2\.2|127\.0\.0\.1)<	Network Security Config permits cleartext traffic: set cleartextTrafficPermitted="false" (allow it only for localhost in a debug-only config)	android/webview/android-webview-tls-bypass.md	nodebug
AND-WV-010	attacker-in-the-middle	high	match	AndroidManifest.xml	android:usesCleartextTraffic="true"	App allows cleartext HTTP: remove usesCleartextTraffic="true" (keep it only in src/debug)	shared/network/attacker-in-the-middle.md	nodebug
AND-WV-011	android-webview-untrusted-content	medium	check	*.kt;*.java	cooccur;;shouldOverrideUrlLoading;;(url|host|uri|Url|Host|Uri)[A-Za-z0-9_.()?!]*\.(contains|startsWith|endsWith)\(	Heuristic: URL allow-list uses substring checks that attacker URLs can satisfy; parse the URL and compare scheme + exact host	android/webview/android-webview-untrusted-content.md	-
AND-WV-012	android-webview-untrusted-content	medium	match	*.kt;*.java	setSafeBrowsingEnabled\([[:space:]]*false|safeBrowsingEnabled[[:space:]]*=[[:space:]]*false	Safe Browsing is disabled for the WebView: keep it enabled	android/webview/android-webview-untrusted-content.md	-
AND-WV-013	android-webview-untrusted-content	medium	check	AndroidManifest.xml	xml_element;;meta-data;;android\.webkit\.WebView\.EnableSafeBrowsing;;android:value="false"	Safe Browsing is disabled app-wide: remove the EnableSafeBrowsing=false meta-data	android/webview/android-webview-untrusted-content.md	-
AND-DLK-001	android-deep-link-abuse	medium	check	AndroidManifest.xml	manifest;;custom_scheme	Custom URL scheme can be claimed by any app: prefer verified https App Links, and validate every deep-link parameter	android/webview/android-deep-link-abuse.md	-
AND-DLK-002	android-deep-link-abuse	medium	check	AndroidManifest.xml	manifest;;applink_no_autoverify	http(s) deep link is not verified: add android:autoVerify="true" and publish assetlinks.json	android/webview/android-deep-link-abuse.md	-
AND-DLK-003	android-deep-link-abuse	high	match	*.kt;*.java	getQueryParameter\(.*loadUrl\(|loadUrl\(.*getQueryParameter\(|loadUrl\([[:space:]]*(intent|getIntent\(\))[.?]*(data|getData|getStringExtra|extras|dataString)	Deep-link input is loaded straight into a WebView: allow-list scheme and host before loading	android/webview/android-deep-link-abuse.md	-
AND-DCL-001	android-dynamic-code-loading	high	match	*.kt;*.java	(DexClassLoader|InMemoryDexClassLoader|PathClassLoader)[[:space:]]*\(|System\.load\(	Code is loaded at runtime: ship code in the APK/AAB (or Play Feature Delivery); never load from writable storage or the network	android/integrity/android-dynamic-code-loading.md	-
AND-DBG-001	android-instrumentation-hooking	high	match	AndroidManifest.xml	android:debuggable="true"	debuggable="true" lets anyone attach a debugger: remove it (the build type sets it)	android/integrity/android-instrumentation-hooking.md	nodebug
AND-DBG-002	android-instrumentation-hooking	high	check	*.gradle;*.gradle.kts;gradle.properties	within;;(^|[^A-Za-z_])release[[:space:]]*\{|getByName\([[:space:]]*"release"[[:space:]]*\)[[:space:]]*\{;;(^|[^A-Za-z])debuggable[[:space:]]*=?[[:space:]]*true|isDebuggable[[:space:]]*=[[:space:]]*true	Release build type is debuggable: remove debuggable/isDebuggable from release	android/integrity/android-instrumentation-hooking.md	-
AND-RE-001	android-reverse-engineering	high	check	*.gradle;*.gradle.kts;gradle.properties	within-absent;;(^|[^A-Za-z_])release[[:space:]]*\{|getByName\([[:space:]]*"release"[[:space:]]*\)[[:space:]]*\{;;minifyEnabled[[:space:]]*=?[[:space:]]*(true|enableProguardInReleaseBuilds)|isMinifyEnabled[[:space:]]*=[[:space:]]*true|optimization[[:space:]]*\{[^}]*enable[[:space:]]*=[[:space:]]*true|^[[:space:]]*enable[[:space:]]*=[[:space:]]*true;;!storeFile|storePassword|keyAlias;;file!dev\.flutter\.flutter-gradle-plugin|flutter_tools/gradle	Release build is not minified/obfuscated: enable R8 (minifyEnabled / isMinifyEnabled = true, or AGP 9 optimization { enable = true }; shrinkResources true) and keep mapping.txt for crash deobfuscation	android/integrity/android-reverse-engineering.md	-
AND-RE-002	android-reverse-engineering	high	match	*.pro;proguard*.txt	^[[:space:]]*-dontobfuscate	-dontobfuscate disables R8 obfuscation: remove it	android/integrity/android-reverse-engineering.md	-
